= My Contribution

As a co-author, I used Python to analyze a 29-year collection of satellite and reanalysis products, including Copernicus SST, DUACS sea-surface height, CERES radiation, NCEP atmospheric fields, and NSIDC sea ice concentration.

= Findings and Publication

We derived Ekman transport from wind stress to examine the Southern Pacific SST dipole and developed a conceptual feedback in which upwelling, sea-ice transport, albedo, and shortwave radiation reinforce regional cooling. The study was published in _STECEP_ in 2024.

